---
import DocsPage from "../../components/DocsPage.astro";

const description = "Turn Mermaid chart syntax and Markdown fences into ChartKit specs and SVG.";
const xy = `xychart-beta
    title "Weekly orders"
    x-axis [Mon, Tue, Wed, Thu, Fri]
    y-axis "Orders"
    bar "Placed" [12, 18, 15, 22, 30]
    line "Shipped" [10, 14, 16, 20, 28]`;
const ts = `import { fromMermaid, toSpec } from "@chartkitdev/core/mermaid";

const { spec, warnings } = fromMermaid(\`${xy}\`);`;
const auto = `import { autoRender } from "@chartkitdev/vanilla/auto";

autoRender(document, { mermaid: true });`;
const html = `<script src="chartkit.global.js" data-chartkit-mermaid></script>
<pre class="mermaid"><code>pie
    title Share of workshop hours
    "Design": 42
    "Build": 35
</code></pre>`;
const remark = `import { rehypeChartkit, remarkChartkit } from "@chartkitdev/markdown";

remark().use(remarkParse).use(remarkChartkit).use(remarkRehype, { allowDangerousHtml: true });
rehype().use(rehypeParse).use(rehypeChartkit);`;
---

<DocsPage title="Use Mermaid or Markdown" description={description} href="/docs/mermaid">
  <p>
    <code>fromMermaid</code> reads chart syntax models already write and returns a v1 spec plus warnings. <code>toSpec</code> accepts that syntax or a ChartKit JSON object. Both live in <code>@chartkitdev/core/mermaid</code> and are not part of the line bundle.
  </p>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>ts</figcaption><pre><code>{ts}</code></pre></figure>
  <h2>Charts</h2>
  <p>Supported Mermaid 11/12 charts:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>xychart</code> and <code>xychart-beta</code>: bar and line series, a title, categories or a numeric x range, and a horizontal bar chart.</li>
    <li><code>pie</code>, including <code>showData</code> (legend values on a pie).</li>
    <li><code>sankey-beta</code> CSV rows.</li>
    <li><code>radar-beta</code>.</li>
    <li><code>treemap-beta</code>.</li>
    <li><code>quadrantChart</code>, drawn as a quadrant. <code>quadrant-1</code> through <code>quadrant-4</code> are top-right, top-left, bottom-left, and bottom-right. An axis <code>Low --&gt; High</code> becomes a <code>Low|High</code> title.</li>
    <li><code>gantt</code> sections, ISO dates, <code>Nd</code>/<code>Nw</code> durations, <code>after id</code>, and done, active, crit, and milestone tags.</li>
    <li><code>timeline</code> years, <code>YYYY-MM</code>, and ISO dates. A slash or dash between two dates is a period. Sections are not date spans.</li>
    <li><code>journey</code> sections, a 1–5 score, and comma-separated actors.</li>
    <li><code>venn-beta</code> <code>set</code> and <code>union</code> lines. Two sets are area-proportional. Three sets are approximate. Text and styles are not drawn.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A frontmatter title, <code>accTitle</code>, and <code>accDescr</code> are read. <code>accDescr</code> or the title becomes <code>a11y.alt</code>. If neither is present, ChartKit writes one factual sentence from the data. Unknown syntax returns a <code>CK8004</code> warning. Flowcharts and other diagrams return <code>CK8003</code> and no spec. <code>gantt</code>, <code>timeline</code>, <code>quadrantChart</code>, <code>venn-beta</code>, and <code>journey</code> load from <code>@chartkitdev/core/mermaid/phase4</code>. <code>fromMermaidAsync</code> loads that chunk, and Node can import <code>fromMermaid</code> from the phase-4 entry directly.
  </p>
  <img src="/mermaid-sheet.png" alt="Mermaid source beside the ChartKit chart for each supported kind, in light mode." />
  <h2>Markdown</h2>
  <p>
    In the browser, <code>autoRender</code> from <code>@chartkitdev/vanilla/auto</code> mounts <code>pre.chartkit</code> and <code>code.language-chartkit</code>. Mermaid fences are opt-in. The shorter <a href="/docs/markdown">Markdown</a> page is the fence overview.
  </p>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>ts</figcaption><pre><code>{auto}</code></pre></figure>
  <p>
    <code>dist/chartkit.global.js</code> draws the core charts and includes <code>ChartKit.autoRender</code>, <code>ChartKit.fromMermaid</code>, and <code>ChartKit.toSpec</code>. <code>dist/chartkit.auto.global.js</code> is auto-render without the Mermaid parser. <code>data-chartkit-mermaid</code> loads the sibling <code>chartkit.mermaid.global.js</code>, which loads <code>chartkit.mermaid-phase4.global.js</code> for gantt, timeline, quadrant, venn, and journey. Histogram through journey load <code>chartkit.&lt;type&gt;.global.js</code> from that same directory. Unsupported Mermaid blocks stay as source.
  </p>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>html</figcaption><pre><code>{html}</code></pre></figure>
  <p>
    <code>@chartkitdev/markdown</code> turns the same fences into server SVG. Pass <code>allowDangerousHtml</code> to remark-rehype so the HTML node is kept.
  </p>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>ts</figcaption><pre><code>{remark}</code></pre></figure>
  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    Column names come from the axis and series titles. One untitled series uses the y-axis title. With no names, the fields are <code>x</code> and <code>value</code>. A line whose scale is far from the bars uses <code>axis: "y2"</code>. A y-axis range on <code>xychart</code> becomes <code>encoding.y.scale.domain</code>. <code>axes.y</code> is display-only. Radar draws a positive max from that domain, still starts at zero, and uses a polygon graticule. A treemap keeps one group level. Quadrant point radius is not drawn. <code>showData</code> prints the value in the legend.
  </p>
  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Fence text is data. The SVG renderer escapes labels, and Mermaid <code>click</code> and <code>href</code> lines are dropped rather than written as links. Sources longer than 100,000 characters are refused (<code>CK8001</code>). Charts keep at most 2,000 points (<code>CK8002</code>). Pass <code>maxSource</code> and <code>maxPoints</code> to change either cap. The global script does not scan Mermaid fences unless the script tag sets <code>data-chartkit-mermaid</code>.
  </p>
</DocsPage>
